  "hypotheses": [
    "H1: Fewer position iterations improve energy retention across initial states, rather than only one initial state.",
    "H2: With external forces every iteration, one full step behaves as v_next=v+h*a(q), q_next=q+h*v+c*h*h*a(q), c=(N+1)/(2*N). No fitted coefficients in the prediction.",
    "H3: Internal position iterations do not recompute generalized gravity from updated angle, so external physical substeps are not equivalent.",
    "H4: Velocity iterations, CPU/GPU, body coordinate-frame choice and energy readout can be ruled in or out as alternate causes.",
    "H5: Small-angle model det(A)=1+(1-c)*k*h*h predicts mean energy growth scale; nonlinear model and long/large-angle tests check limits."
  ],
